{
	title: 'Web client buttons and cards use inline SVG icons',
	spec: "src/web/icons.ts holds the web client icons as inline SVG markup generated from upstream files: Phosphor Regular (MIT) except steer (Tabler arrow-ramp-right, MIT) and python (IconPark snake-zodiac, Apache 2.0); all three licence notices sit in that file. components/Icon.tsx renders one decoratively (aria-hidden); the surrounding control keeps the accessible name. index.html sets one stroke width (--icon-stroke: 1.5, in 24-grid units) for both grids. Composer buttons are icon-only with aria-labels and tooltips: attach (paper clip), pause/continue, queue, steer, send, run (lightning) and attachment remove. The prompt edit button is a simple pencil; folded thinking cards show a flask (Phosphor flask), messages from other sessions the send tool's speech bubble, and tool cards an icon for their tool (a bash card whose command starts Python in command position, such as python3 or cd x && python3 -, shows a snake instead of the terminal; command and slash-command run use a lightning bolt; bash, read, read_url, google, send, spawn, wait, command, inspect, notify, ask, read_blob). Close buttons use an x; text buttons (kill, undo, show all/less, tab menu, new tab, notify, notifications, diagnostics, reload, logout, answer, cancel, apply, rebase and notification controls) gain a leading icon and keep their text. Web only: the terminal keeps its text glyphs; ask before changing it.",
	status: 'done',
	notes: [
		'icons.ts is generated by a throwaway script from the upstream raw SVGs (phosphor-icons/core raw/regular, tabler-icons icons/outline): it strips the 256 background rect, replaces the repeated stroke attributes with class "s" and keeps filled dots as fills. Phosphor strokes are 16 units on a 256 grid, so CSS scales --icon-stroke by 256/24. Buttons drop the literal space after the icon; CSS gap spaces them, so textContent stays the label (a browser test reads it).',
		'Composer layout: attach sits left of the draft (DOM first, so tab order matches); the right side holds a narrow 36px pause/continue toggle, then queue and steer while a turn runs, or send when idle; steer/send uses the accent colour. Pause stays reachable while typing and continue while editing. A combined steer/queue button is a planned follow-up. Terminal decision (user): the terminal stays mostly ASCII/Unicode text, not icons.',
		'Python detection was checked against bash commands in the 50 most recent sessions: 441 mention python; the command-position regex matches 440 (the miss runs no Python). Forms: python3 - <<EOF heredoc 386, -c 39, script.py 11, -m 1. One false positive quoted ; python3 inside a tsk spec string; acceptable.'
	],
	needs: ['wwf']
}
